  "limitations": [
    "Each run rebuilds release artifacts from the one pinned source commit, so the spread includes build-to-build as well as runner-to-runner variation; that is the variation a real candidate run carries.",
    "Run 36078460497 is the beta.8 baseline run, dispatched from benchmarks ref beta8/core-closeout-arrival-families; the other five were dispatched from develop. The core commit, workload profiles, repetitions, runner image (ubuntu-24.04 20260920.314.1) and per-surface OS kernel and runtimes are identical across all six.",
    "The spread is dominated by runner hardware, not by rerun noise: runs 36078460497, 36177107404, 36177116881 and 36177124781 agree within 6.4% on every processing median, while 36177797166 measured about 22% and 36177805247 about 45% faster on every surface and profile at once. Region does not explain it (eastus hosted both a slow and a fast run), and the job log does not record the CPU model, so a run's hardware class cannot be identified from its evidence.",
    "Not a derivation source: two times this spread (183% processing, 177% initialization) would set every latency and initialization threshold near 185% and erase both detector-expansion regressions the backtest flags. The budgets therefore stay proposed until timing is bound to an identified runner hardware class or measured paired within one job."
  ]
